# Rogue's Passage: "{4}, {T}: Target creature can't be blocked this turn." (CR 509.1b, 611.2a). Bot1 casts Grizzly Bears on
# turn 1, plays the Passage on turn 3 and pays the {4} with Black Lotus and Mox Sapphire (the pool empty afterwards) and the
# {T} with the land itself, so the Bears attacks unblocked - the Elves may not block it - and Bot2 takes 2. A noncreature
# permanent is refused as the target. On turn 5 the restriction has ended - the Elves blocks the same Bears and Bot2 takes
# nothing more.

